.Dd $Mdocdate: February 13 2025 $
.Dt STD-DEFAULT 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm std-default
.Nd automate standard set collection
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
set collection provides common rules, macros, and useful constants to
standardize
.Xr automate 1
scripts.
.Ss MACROS
.Bl -tag -width XXXXXXXXXXX -compact
.It %%glob-edit
A macro to the common pattern of globbing followed by an edit.
.El
.Ss CONSTANTS
.Bl -tag -width XXXXXXXXXX -compact
.It %host-arch
The architecture of the host system.
.It %host-os
The operating system of the host system.
.El
.Ss VIRTUAL RULES
.Bl -tag -width XXXXXXXX -compact
.It @etc
Configuration files.
.It @data
Data resources.
.It @include
Headers.
.It @libexec
Helper executables.
.It @library
Libraries.
.It @program
Executables.
.It @manpage
Manual pages.
.El
.Ss RULES
.Bl -tag -width XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX -compact
.It all
Build all project artifacts.
.It clean
Delete all generated files and build outputs.
.It install
Install all targets to system directories.
.It install-etc
Install configuration files.
.It install-data
Install data resources.
.It install-include
Install header files.
.It install-libexec
Install helper executables.
.It install-library
Install libraries.
.It install-program
Install executables.
.It install-manpage
Install manual pages.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XXXXXXXXXXX
.It BINDIR
Installation directory for executables.
.It BINPERM
Permissions for installed executables.
.It DESTDIR
Root directory for staged installations.
.It DRTDIR
Data resource directory.
.It DRTPERM
Permissions for data resources.
.It ETCDIR
Configuration directory.
.It ETCPERM
Permissions for configuration files.
.It LIBDIR
Library installation directory.
.It LIBPERM
Permissions for libraries.
.It LIBEXECDIR
Helper executables directory.
.It LIBEXECPERM
Permissions for helper executables.
.It MANDIR
Manual page directory.
.It MANPERM
Permissions for manual pages.
.It PREFIX
Base installation directory.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX -compact
.It Pa Ev AUTOMATE_ETC_DIR Ns /env/std-default
Configuration file containing default values for all environment variables.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
To set program through the macro:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
@program{
	transform{
		${%%glob-edit}
		edit:sed "s;.c$$;;"
		glob:src/*.c
	}
}
.Ed
